      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "When you have BOTH an indirect and",
          "direct object pronoun together:",
          "",
          "ORDER: indirect THEN direct          Press 1",
          "",
          "Me lo dio. (He gave it to me.)",
          "Te la compré. (I bought it for you.)",
          "Nos los trajeron. (They brought them to us.",
          "",
          "THE SE RULE:                         Press 2",
          "",
          "When le/les meets lo/la/los/las,",
          "le/les becomes SE:",
          "",
          "Le di el libro → Se lo di.",
          "(I gave him the book → I gave it to him.)",
          "",
          "NOT: Le lo di. Always SE lo/la/los."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lección veintisiete",
